From af75c1d1ec6938c233797f6f36f49e13d63f5803 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:47:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0038-vela-ue-xess-depth: port of upstream OptiScaler 7e94156
 (2026-11-17, Extract depth and MVs for XeSS inputs in Unreal Engine games; no
 follow-up fixes upstream up to 2026-11-22): in an Unreal game the XeSS input
 finds the UE XeSS plugin's velocity flattening (texture names Upscaled
 Velocity Texture / XeSS::FlattenedVelocity / XeSS::UpscaledVelocity in the
 exe or an *xess* module), records its SceneDepth FRDGTexture, resolves the
 ID3D12Resource behind it and copies it (R32F, DS shader) in queue order right
 before the command list that runs XeSS; only an XeSS execute without depth
 gets the copy (DepthInverted set for it, OptiScaler.DepthState =
 NON_PIXEL_SHADER_RESOURCE, honoured by SGSR 2 / SGSR 3 / frame generation).
 ARM64EC changes: no SEH (VirtualQuery-checked reads), local scanner helpers
 with the function start from the game's x64 .pdata, a present-counted release
 queue instead of DeferredRelease. VELA_UE_XESS_DEPTH=0 = off (default on);
 upstream's render-size motion vectors (GetSecondaryViewRectSize hook,
 bUpsample=false) are opt-in with VELA_UE_XESS_RENDER_MV=1. Vela depth lines:
 capture on/off once, plugin not found once, per XeSS context: copy used
 (size, format), stopped / back, not found in 120 frames

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
